st += [P('3.3 Software Development','H2x'),P('The firmware sampled the sensors, applied local threshold logic, displayed status on the ST7789, drove the buzzer and RGB outputs, logged to SD and queued readings for later synchronization. The backend exposed authenticated REST endpoints, persisted patients, sessions, readings, alerts and device health in PostgreSQL, and enforced idempotent device-event handling. The React dashboard obtained KPI values and trends from the API.','Bodyx'),P('The AI pipeline generated simulated monitoring sessions, trained an exploratory model and stored model/report artifacts. The backend could load the model in prototype mode, but threshold alerts remained independent of model availability. This separation prevented an unavailable or experimental AI component from disabling local safety alerts.','Bodyx'),P('3.4 Testing','H2x'),P('The firmware evidence recorded successful compilation and upload for the ESP32-S3. The dedicated RGB and SD diagnostic recorded four passing operations, including repeated write/read/append/compare/delete checks. The display and sensor diagnostic reported a partial pass: the display operated and the firmware ran, while heart-rate estimates remained unstable and accuracy was not established.','Bodyx'),P('The repository also contained API and database tests for authentication, access control, patient/device/session creation, device synchronization, deduplication, stored history and alert handling. These results were used as software evidence; the hosted API itself was not reachable reliably during report generation, so no unavailable hosted metric was presented as a measured result.','Bodyx'),PageBreak()]
st += [P('3.5 Evaluation','H1x'),P('The proposal specified sampling accuracy, sampling period and jitter, local alert latency, synchronization performance, AI false-alarm rate and detection lead time, backend response time, security checks, end-to-end delay, timekeeping drift and continuous operation. The available evidence supported implementation and integration claims, but it did not support clinical accuracy claims or a complete AI baseline comparison. The report therefore separated measured prototype checks from metrics that remained pending controlled data collection.','Bodyx'),P('3.6 Results by Specific Objective','H1x')]
data=[['Specific objective','How it was obtained','Result and evidence'],['Hardware design','A KiCad schematic assigned every sensor, display, SD, RTC, alarm and RGB signal to named ESP32-S3 nets. The two-layer PCB was routed from that connectivity.','Achieved at prototype integration level. Schematic ERC and PCB DRC reports recorded zero violations, zero unrouted items and zero schematic-parity differences for the validated SPI carrier revision.'],['Software development','Firmware, FastAPI/Flask-compatible API services, PostgreSQL models, AI artifacts and React views were implemented. Offline readings were queued and synchronized by event identity.','Achieved as a working prototype. Repository tests and firmware logs documented successful build, upload, SD operations, API flow and dashboard data paths.'],['Testing','Separate diagnostics exercised display/sensors, RGB, SD, firmware build/upload, API behavior and integrated dataflow.','Partially achieved. Build/upload and SD diagnostics passed; display operation passed. Heart-rate stability and clinical accuracy remained unverified.'],['Evaluation','The project defined error, jitter, latency, synchronization, AI baseline and backend metrics and compared available evidence with those targets.','Partially achieved. Prototype implementation evidence was available; complete controlled AI false-alarm/lead-time and clinical accuracy datasets were not available.']]
t=Table([[P(c,'Smallx') for c in row] for row in data],colWidths=[35*mm,72*mm,68*mm],repeatRows=1);t.setStyle(TableStyle([('BACKGROUND',(0,0),(-1,0),colors.HexColor('#17324d')),('TEXTCOLOR',(0,0),(-1,0),colors.white),('GRID',(0,0),(-1,-1),.35,colors.HexColor('#9aa')),('VALIGN',(0,0),(-1,-1),'TOP'),('BACKGROUND',(0,1),(-1,-1),colors.HexColor('#f2f6f8')),('LEFTPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),5),('RIGHTPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),5)]));st += [t,Spacer(1,5*mm),P('The four objectives formed one chain: the hardware allocated reliable sensing and local alert paths; the software captured and interpreted those signals; testing verified the interfaces and dataflow; evaluation identified which performance claims were supported and which required further controlled experiments. Together, these stages produced the final offline-first monitoring prototype.','Bodyx')]
